{"content":[{"c":["AMORITES, HILL COUNTRY (MOUNT*) OF THE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Central mountainous region between the plains of Philistia, Sharon, and Phoenicia on the west and the valley of the Jordan on the east. While the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," uses “mount,” most modern translations use “hill country” because the phrase does not denote a single mountain but the range running north and south through Judah and Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.7,19-20","r":"Deut.1.7,19-20","rawR":"Deut.1.7,19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.7,19-20","value":"Deut.1.7,19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 1:7, 19-20"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AmoritesHillCountryMountofthe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 1:7, 19-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.1.7,19-20","rawQueryValue":"Deut.1.7,19-20","sourceRefExact":"Deut.1.7,19-20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"baad7497e92aeb2a75a6eb66e7ce355419322510d56b136fcef931322b11dbe5","sourceItemName":"AmoritesHillCountryMountofthe","sourceItemOrder":312,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AmoritesHillCountryMountofthe","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Amorites, Hill Country (Mount*) of the","title":"Amorites, Hill Country (Mount*) of the","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}